{"count":1095,"next":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=4&page_size=100","previous":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=2&page_size=100","results":[{"id":406,"title":"AFP Chief Welcomes, Fetes Troops from BRP Sierra Madre","slug":"afp-chief-welcomes-fetes-troops-from-brp-sierra-madre","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr., Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), welcomed and awarded the 28 military personnel who were stationed at BRP Sierra Madre today, July 29 at Naval Detachment Oyster Bay Pier in Puerto Princesa, Palawan.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/BRP.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, receives the returning Navy personnel who have completed their deployment at the BRP Sierra Madre on Ayungin Shoal on July 29, 2024, at Naval Detachment Oyster Bay Pier, Palawan.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-29T09:31:45+08:00","hits":225},{"id":407,"title":"Philippine ROTC Games Luzon-NCR Opens in Cavite","slug":"philippine-rotc-games-luzon-ncr-opens-in-cavite","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Luzon and National Capital Region leg of the 2024 Philippine Reserve Officers Training Corps (ROTC) Games officially commenced today, July 28, at Cavite State University (CvSU).</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/ROTC.jpg","image_caption":"Participants recite the oath of sportsmanship during the opening of the Luzon Leg of the Philippine ROTC games on July 28 in Cavite.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-28T09:29:59+08:00","hits":337},{"id":408,"title":"Statement of General Romeo S Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, on the One Meal Subsistence Allowance donation of AFP members to victims of Typhoon Carina","slug":"statement-of-general-romeo-s-brawner-jr-chief-of-staff-of-the-armed-forces-of-the-philippines-on-the-one-meal-subsistence-allowance-donation-of-afp-members-to-victims-of-typhoon-carina","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) is extending its support to the victims of Typhoon Carina by donating the equivalent of one meal from their Subsistence Allowance, amounting to P50.00 per member. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/subs.jpg","image_caption":"On One Meal Subsistence Allowance donation of AFP members to victims of Typhoon Carina","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-27T09:26:42+08:00","hits":176},{"id":409,"title":"AFP Intensifies HADR Operations for Typhoon Carina Victims","slug":"afp-intensifies-hadr-operations-for-typhoon-carina-victims","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) is actively engaged in extensive Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Response (HADR) operations following the impact of Typhoon Carina and the southwest monsoon.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/HADR%201.jpg","image_caption":"⁨⁨Rescued residents aboard a rubber boat during the Army's rescue efforts in Tinajeros, Malabon on July 24, 2024.⁩⁩  (Photo by 525th Engineer Battalion)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-26T09:47:55+08:00","hits":623},{"id":410,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff welcomes US Chief of Naval Operations","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-welcomes-us-chief-of-naval-operations","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City –General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), met with Admiral Lisa Franchetti, Chief of Naval Operations of the United States Navy, during the latter's courtesy visit on July 26, 2024, at the AFP General Headquarters here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/EXC2.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, AFP Chief of Staff, and Admiral Lisa Franchetti, U.S. Navy Chief of Operations, exchange insights during the latter’s courtesy visit on July 26, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-26T07:39:50+08:00","hits":249},{"id":411,"title":"AFP Mobilizes for Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Relief (HADR) Amid Habagat, Typhoon Carina","slug":"afp-mobilizes-for-humanitarian-assistance-and-disaster-relief-hadr-amid-habagat-typhoon-carina","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – In response to the devastating impact of Typhoon Carina and Habagat, the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) has launched extensive Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Relief (HADR) operations across the affected regions.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/HADR2%201.jpg","image_caption":"The PAF 505th SRG team rescues families affected by flooding in Barangay 183, Pasay City.  (Photo by 505th SRG)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-24T09:42:51+08:00","hits":491},{"id":412,"title":"Statement re 3rd SONA of PBBM","slug":"statement-re-3rd-sona-of-pbbm","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We heard President Ferdinand Marcos Jr.'s call to not yield in the defense and protection of our territory and sovereign rights. This is a call that will always be heeded by those in the profession of arms, a duty and mandate that will always rally the brave sons and daughters of our nation.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/AFP3SONA%201.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Statement regarding 3rd State of the Nation Address of President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr. ","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-23T09:36:39+08:00","hits":268},{"id":413,"title":"AFP Welcomes New PMA Superintendent, honors outgoing General","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-pma-superintendent-honors-outgoing-general","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) welcomed Rear Admiral Caesar Bernard N. Valencia PN as the new Superintendent of the Philippine Military Academy (PMA) in a ceremony held on July 20, 2024 in Fort Del Pilar, Baguio City.<br /></span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/PMA%201.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA, AFP Chief of Staff passes over the Command Saber to Rear Admiral Caesar Bernard N Valencia PN, the incoming PMA Superintendent from Lieutenant General Rowen S Tolentino PA during the change of command ceremony in Fort Del Pilar, Baguio City on July 20, 2024. (Photo by SSg Ambay PA/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-20T09:07:32+08:00","hits":1517},{"id":414,"title":"AFP all set for PBBM’s 3rd SONA, ensures peace and security","slug":"afp-all-set-for-pbbm-s-3rd-sona-ensures-peace-and-security","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), through the Joint Task Force-NCR, deployed around 500 personnel and two armored vehicles in support of the Philippine National Police (PNP) for the upcoming 3rd State of the Nation Address (SONA) of President Ferdinand Marcos Jr on July 22, 2024.<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The send-off ceremony was held at the Headquarters of the Quezon City Police District at Camp Karingal today. Part of the activity is the blessing of the security forces contingent and assets to be deployed.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The AFP remains steadfast in supporting the PNP and ensuring a secure and peaceful SONA of the President. Through collaborative efforts and unwavering dedication, the AFP stands ready to safeguard the nation's stability and democratic proceedings.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Photo by Joint Task Force-NCR</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/viber_image_2024-07-19_17-27-42-388.jpg","image_caption":"Members of the Joint Task Force-NCR stand in formation during the send-off ceremony for SONA 2024 on July 19 at Camp Karingal, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-19T09:04:48+08:00","hits":288},{"id":415,"title":"AFPETDC Celebrates 7th Anniversary","slug":"afpetdc-celebrates-7th-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City –The Armed Forces of the Philippines Education, Training, and Doctrine Command (AFPETDC) celebrated its 7th founding anniversary on July 18, 2024, here. The event was graced by General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, as Guest of Honor and Speaker.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/ETDC4.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff and Senator Mark Villar leads the ribbon-cutting ceremony of the newly built study barracks during the AFPETDC 7th anniversary on July 18, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-18T16:28:20+08:00","hits":876},{"id":416,"title":"AFP holds the 2024 Dependents Sports League Closing Ceremony","slug":"afp-holds-the-2024-dependents-sports-league-closing-ceremony","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City –The Armed Forces of the Philippines held the closing ceremony for the 2024 Dependents Sports League, on July 18, 2024, here. LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, the AFP Deputy Chief of Staff, graced the event as Guest of Honor and Speaker on behalf of General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/sf.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, TDCSAFP, and participants pose for a photo during 2024 Dependents Sports League closing ceremony on July 18, 2024","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-18T09:30:50+08:00","hits":300},{"id":417,"title":"AFP welcomes Indonesia's Resilience Institute delegates","slug":"afp-welcomes-indonesias-resilience-institute-delegates","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Vice Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Arthur Cordura PAF, received the 32-member delegation from the National Resilience Institute of the Republic of Indonesia (Lemhannas) led by Air Vice Marshall Hesly Paat, in a courtesy visit on July 17, 2024, here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/viber_image_2024-07-17_18-13-12-819.jpg","image_caption":"Air Vice Marshall Hesly Paat receives a token of appreciation from LtGen Arthur Cordura, VCSAFP, during a courtesy visit on July 17, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-17T09:26:08+08:00","hits":197},{"id":418,"title":"CSAFP dons new rank to two senior officers","slug":"csafp-dons-new-rank-to-two-senior-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City— The Commander of Eastern Mindanao Command (EASTMINCOM), MGen Luis Rex Bergante PA, and the AFP's The Provost Marshal General (TPMG), Col Ferdinand Marcelino PN(M) were promoted to the next higher rank in a ceremony with the AFP Chief General Romeo Brawner Jr., here today.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/DON4%201.jpg","image_caption":"AFP renders arrival honors to the newly promoted BGen Ferdinand Marcelino PN(M), The Provost Marshal General, following the donning of ranks ceremony on July 17, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-17T09:21:01+08:00","hits":468},{"id":419,"title":"PH-US military chiefs tout strong military alliance","slug":"ph-us-military-chiefs-tout-strong-military-alliance","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff, General Romeo Brawner Jr., hosted a high-level meeting with United States Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, General Charles Q. Brown Jr., on July 16 at the AFP General Headquarters here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/ALL4.jpg","image_caption":"Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff, General Romeo Brawner Jr., hands over a memento to United States Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, General Charles Q. Brown Jr., after their meeting on July 16 at the AFP General Headquarters, Quezon City.  (Photo by SSg Ambay/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-16T14:09:59+08:00","hits":475},{"id":420,"title":"AFP welcomes the Australian Command and Staff College Delegates","slug":"afp-welcomes-the-australian-command-and-staff-college-delegates","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Lieutenant Colonel Alister Eric Sparkes and 13 other students from the Australian Command and Staff College paid a courtesy call on BGen Krishnamurti Mortela PA, Assistant Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training, and Doctrine, AJ8, during their study tour at the AFP General Headquarters on July 16.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/451739494_860981432730935_1628069680040653311_n.jpg","image_caption":"BGen Krishnamurti Mortela PA, Assistant DCS for Education, Training, and Doctrine, AJ8, and Lt Col. Alister Eric Sparkes, sit in discussion during a courtesy visit on July 16, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-16T14:07:56+08:00","hits":300},{"id":421,"title":"AFP, PNP, PCG conduct 2nd Quarter 2024 JPSCC Meeting","slug":"afp-pnp-pcg-conduct-2nd-quarter-2024-jpscc-meeting","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP CRAME, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), the Philippine Coast Guard (PCG), and the Philippine National Police (PNP) conducted the 2nd Quarter 2024 National Joint Peace and Security Coordinating Center (JPSCC) Meeting on July 11 at the PNP Headquarters in Quezon City.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/jpscc.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr, PNP Director General PGen Rommel Francisco Marbil, and PCG Commandant Admiral Ronnie Gil Gavan present a signed joint resolution during the 2nd Quarter 2024 National Joint Peace and Security Coordinating Center Meeting on July 11 at the PNP Headquarters in Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-11T14:01:24+08:00","hits":2099},{"id":422,"title":"CSAFP sends off new defense, armed forces attachés","slug":"csafp-sends-off-new-defense-armed-forces-attaches","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, met with the new defense and armed forces attachés (DAFA) during a courtesy visit on July 11 at the General Headquarters here.<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The call is an avenue for the CSAFP to give his guidance to the officers, who will work to enhance the AFP's defense and military relations with their host nations. They will also serve as the point of contact on defense and security-related matters.<br /><br /><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">The deployment is part of the AFP's commitment to promoting good will with other nations as part of the AFP's international defense and security engagements.<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Photo by SSg Ambay/PAOAFP</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/DAF2.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr meets with Captain Arnold Fortin, the incoming Defense and Armed Forces Attache (DAFA) to China, and two new DAFAs during their courtesy call on July 11 at the AFP General Headquarters in Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-11T13:59:21+08:00","hits":384},{"id":423,"title":"AFP Installs New JTF-NCR Commander","slug":"afp-installs-new-jtf-ncr-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines formally installed BGen Eric Macaambac PN(M) as the new Joint Task Force National Capital (JTF-NCR) Commander in a Change of Command Ceremony presided over by AFP Chief of Staff, General Romeo Brawner Jr., on July 10, 2024, here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/dd.jpg","image_caption":"BGen Eric Macaambac incoming JTF-NCR Commander, receives the symbol of leadership from AFP Chief of Staff, General Romeo Brawner Jr., during the Change of Command Ceremony on July 10, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-10T13:57:22+08:00","hits":1177},{"id":424,"title":"AFP Honors the 7th Anniversary of the Philippine Rise","slug":"afp-honors-the-7th-anniversary-of-the-philippine-rise","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines joined the Naval Forces Northern Luzon (NFNL) to commemorate the 7th anniversary of the Philippine Rise especially in upholding the nation’s sovereignty and territorial integrity on July 9, 2024, at PPIC 1, Poro Point, San Fernando, La Union.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/PRISE2.jpg","image_caption":"Naval Forces Northern Luzon salute over the Philippine flag aboard FF150 during the 7th Anniversary of the Philippine Rise on July 9, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-10T13:55:55+08:00","hits":340},{"id":425,"title":"CSAFP Welcomes Brazillian Ambassador","slug":"csafp-welcomes-brazillian-ambassador","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, welcomed His Excellency Gilberto Fonseca Guimarães de Moura, Ambassador of Brazil to the Philippines in a courtesy visit on July 9, here, to foster deeper defense relations.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/BRA2.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, and His Excellency Gilberto Fonseca Guimarães de Moura, Ambassador of Brazil to the Philippines, during the latter’s courtesy call on July 9, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-09T14:31:44+08:00","hits":268},{"id":426,"title":"CSAFP joins PH-JP 2+2 meeting, lauds RAA signing","slug":"csafp-joins-ph-jp-2-2-meeting-lauds-raa-signing","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo Brawner Jr., joined in the 2+2 meeting between the Philippines and Japan on July 8.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/viber_image_2024-07-08_20-33-57-359.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr and Japan Self-Defense Force Chief of Joint Staff General Yoshihide Yoshida meet ahead of the 2nd PH-Japan Foreign and Defense Ministerial Meeting (2+2) held on July 8, 2024, in Taguig City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-08T14:29:51+08:00","hits":244},{"id":427,"title":"President Marcos Jr visits 11th Infantry Division in Sulu","slug":"president-marcos-jr-visits-11th-infantry-division-in-sulu","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. visited the 11th Infantry Division in Sulu on July 5 to engage with the troops and express his support for their ongoing efforts to maintain peace and security in the region.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/viber_image_2024-07-05_19-35-23-309.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand Marcos Jr talks to the troops of the 11th Infantry Division, Philippine Army during his visit to their headquarters in Sulu on July 5.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-05T14:27:39+08:00","hits":245},{"id":428,"title":"CSAFP announces Philippine Flag to be part of AFP Battle Dress Uniform","slug":"csafp-announces-philippine-flag-to-be-part-of-afp-battle-dress-uniform","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, announced the Philippine Flag patch to be an integral part of the AFP-wide battle dress uniform during a press conference on July 4, highlighting a significant symbol of national pride.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/PAT3.jpg","image_caption":"Military personnel dons Philippine Flag patch on their battle dress uniform as a visible reminder of AFP's commitment to upholding the Philippine sovereign rights and territorial integrity. (Photo by PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-04T15:19:37+08:00","hits":4051},{"id":429,"title":"AFP presses fight against WPS misinformation with Complan “Mulat”","slug":"afp-presses-fight-against-wps-misinformation-with-complan-mulat","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -- In line with its ongoing efforts to safeguard national sovereignty and promote regional stability, the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) has introduced the \"Mulat\" Communication Plan for the West Philippine Sea.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/MUL1.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo S Brawner Jr addresses the media at Tejeros Hall, Camp Aguinaldo, unveiling the AFP's Communication Plan \"Mulat\" aimed at safeguarding the nation's maritime rights and interests. (Photo by LTC JP Salgado (PA) / PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-04T14:20:53+08:00","hits":1655},{"id":430,"title":"AFP honors LtGen Tolentino during Exit Call","slug":"afp-honors-ltgen-tolentino-during-exit-call","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines rendered arrival honors to LtGen Rowen Tolentino, Superintendent of the Philippine Military Academy, during his exit call on July 4, 2024, here.<br /></span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/ECALL.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, and PMA Superintendent, LtGen Rowen Tolentino, during the latter’s exit call on July 4, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-04T12:26:59+08:00","hits":1186},{"id":431,"title":"CSAFP Welcomes Royal Thai Navy Commander-in-Chief","slug":"csafp-welcomes-royal-thai-navy-commander-in-chief","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, welcomed Admiral Adoong Pan-lam, Commander-in-Chief, Royal Thai Navy, during his courtesy call on July 4, 2024, here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/CCALL.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, and Admiral Adoong Pan-lam, Commander-in-Chief, Royal Thai Navy, sit in discussion during the latter’s courtesy call on July 4, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-04T12:25:29+08:00","hits":790},{"id":432,"title":"AFP Hosts Mid-Year Command Conference with President Marcos Jr","slug":"afp-hosts-mid-year-command-conference-with-president-marcos-jr","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) held its mid-year Command Conference on July 4, with Commander-in-Chief President Ferdinand Marcos Jr attending to review the progress of AFP’s campaigns and programs for the first semester and to provide further directives.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/COMCON5.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand Marcos Jr is accorded with arrival honors led by General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff during the 1st Semester 2024 AFP Command Conference on July 04 at Tejeros Hall, AFPCOC, CGEA.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-04T12:19:17+08:00","hits":717},{"id":433,"title":"AFP holds BUKAL special screening, a thrive for peace","slug":"afp-holds-bukal-special-screening-a-thrive-for-peace","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City— The Armed Forces of the Philippines hosted a special screening of an award-winning film, “BUKAL,” which was graced by Senator Robin Padilla and LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, the Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, on July 3, here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/BUKAL2.jpg","image_caption":"Senator Robin Padilla and LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, the Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, during the “BUKAL” special screening on July 3, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-04T12:17:38+08:00","hits":559},{"id":434,"title":"AFP fetes UN observers, staff","slug":"afp-fetes-un-observers-staff","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) held a recognition ceremony during Monday's flag-raising rites on July 1 here to honor the exemplary service of officers assigned at the United Nations and its peacekeeping missions.<br /></span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/July%202024/UNO3.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP, awards the UN Service Medal to LtCol Andy Raymundo during the awarding and flag-raising ceremony on July 1 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-07-01T12:14:42+08:00","hits":595},{"id":435,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff commends Citizen Reserve Force graduates, emphasizes crucial role in territorial defense","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-commends-citizen-reserve-force-graduates-emphasizes-crucial-role-in-territorial-defense","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – General Romeo S. Brawner Jr., the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), lauded the graduates of the Basic Citizen Military Course Class 08-24 01 and 09-24 during the closing ceremony held at the Baguio Country Club on Saturday, June 29, 2024.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/RES.jpg","image_caption":"New graduates of the Basic Citizen Military Course will join the Naval Forces Reserve-Northern Luzon. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-29T09:19:13+08:00","hits":833},{"id":436,"title":"AFP Renders Testimonial Parade and Review in honor of retiring PMA Cavaliers","slug":"afp-renders-testimonial-parade-and-review-in-honor-of-retiring-pma-cavaliers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) rendered a testimonial parade and review in honor of retiring cavaliers at the Philippine Military Academy (PMA) in Baguio City on Saturday, June 29.<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The honored retirees were Major General Proceso S. Rebancos PA, the Chief Engineer of the AFP and a member of PMA Class 1994; Brigadier General Federico B. Enriquez PAF, Wing Commander of Tactical Operations Wing Central and a member of PMA Class 1993; Brigadier General Romeo T. Racadio PN(M), Deputy Commander of the Philippine Marine Corps; and Coast Guard Rear Admiral Rudyard M. Somera, Director of the Coast Guard Strategic Studies and International Affairs Center and a member of PMA Class 1992.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/PMA.jpg","image_caption":"From left: Coast Guard RAdm Rudyard M. Somera, Director of the Coast Guard Strategic Studies and International Affairs Center; MGen Proceso S. Rebancos PA, the Chief Engineer of the AFP; BGen Romeo T. Racadio PN(M), Deputy Commander of the Philippine Marine Corps; and BGen Federico B. Enriquez PAF, Wing Commander of Tactical Operations Wing Central were rendered retirement honors at the Philippine Military Academy in Baguio City on June 29, 2024. (Photo by: PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-29T09:15:40+08:00","hits":1544},{"id":437,"title":"AFP Unveils WPS Mulat, Reinforce Maritime Rights","slug":"afp-unveils-wps-mulat-reinforce-maritime-rights","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) proudly launched the WPS MULAT cover photo on June 28, here, headed by General Romeo Brawner Jr., Chief of Staff of the AFP, signifying ongoing efforts to enhance transparency, awareness, and strategic communication for the West Philippines Sea (WPS).</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/MUL.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, along with senior AFP officials, officially launches the WPS MULAT during a ceremony on June 28, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-29T09:13:27+08:00","hits":1244},{"id":438,"title":"AFP Medical Service Commemorates 126th Anniversary","slug":"afp-medical-service-commemorates-126th-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Medical Service celebrated its 126th founding anniversary June 28 in a ceremony held at the Tejeros Hall here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/4.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP; BGen Fatima Claire Navarro, The AFP Surgeon General; and Col Jose Rosel Reduble, The Deputy Surgeon General AFP pose for a photo with the outstanding personnel of the AFP Medical Service during their 126th founding anniversary celebration on June 28 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-28T09:10:05+08:00","hits":671},{"id":439,"title":"AFP Statement | On the alarming surge in disinformation efforts.","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-alarming-surge-in-disinformation-efforts","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/STADIS.jpg","image_caption":"Statement of the Armed Forces of the Philippines on the alarming surge in disinformation efforts.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-28T01:04:53+08:00","hits":677},{"id":440,"title":"WESCOM commander, 3 other senior officers promoted","slug":"wescom-commander-3-other-senior-officers-promoted","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--Rear Admiral Alfonso Torres Jr, Commander of Western Command (WESCOM), received his third star in a donning of ranks ceremony on June 27 at the General Headquarters here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/3SEN2.jpg","image_caption":"Newly promoted Vice Admiral Alfonso Torres Jr, Commander of Western Command, receives military honors led by MGen Jeffrey Hechanova, The Deputy Chief of Staff for Plans, J5, after the donning of ranks ceremony on June 27 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.  Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-27T09:02:22+08:00","hits":1365},{"id":441,"title":"CSAFP Welcomes New Defense and Armed Forces Attachés","slug":"csafp-welcomes-new-defense-and-armed-forces-attaches","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, welcomed new Defense and Armed Forces Attachés (DAFA) on June 26 at the General Headquarters here, marking their new diplomatic missions.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/ATT2.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, poses for a photo with incoming Defense and Armed Forces Attachés during a courtesy call on June 26, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-26T08:59:57+08:00","hits":1201},{"id":442,"title":"President Marcos lauds troops for bravery, dedication in visit to WESCOM","slug":"president-marcos-lauds-troops-for-bravery-dedication-in-visit-to-wescom","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. visited the AFP Western Command today to personally check on the troops involved in the June 17 incident with the China Coast Guard during a Rotation and Resupply mission for the BRP Sierra Madre at Ayungin Shoal.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/BBMWES%201.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr., poses for a photo with personnel of the AFP Western Command on June 23.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-23T10:35:38+08:00","hits":863},{"id":443,"title":"AFP Statement on the Expression of Support by the Philippine Business Groups","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-expression-of-support-by-the-philippine-business-groups","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">The men and women of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) stand humbled and grateful for the unwavering support expressed by the Philippine Business Groups.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/PBG%201.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-23T10:32:00+08:00","hits":724},{"id":444,"title":"CSAFP: ‘OUR TROOPS FOUGHT BACK’","slug":"csafp-our-troops-fought-back","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, said that soldiers conducting a rotation and resupply mission at the BRP Sierra Madre (LS57) at Ayungin Shoal on June 17 fought back with “everything that they had.”</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/OTFB2.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, pins an award to the wounded Navy personnel on June 19 who was part of the rotation and resupply mission at the BRP Sierra Madre in Ayungin Shoal on June 17.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-20T11:41:32+08:00","hits":1718},{"id":445,"title":"AFP, JSDF voice concern over Chinese aggression in WPS","slug":"afp-jsdf-voice-concern-over-chinese-aggression-in-wps","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines and the Japan Self-Defense Forces jointly voiced their concern on the recent developments in the West Philippine Sea given China’s recent escalation at Ayungin Shoal.</span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/JSDF1.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the AFP, during his meeting with General Yoshihide Yoshida, Chief of Joint Staff JSDF, via video teleconference on June 20.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-20T10:24:51+08:00","hits":791},{"id":446,"title":"VIDEOS | Incident during RoRe mission on June 17","slug":"video-incident-during-rore-mission-on-june-17","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">In a brazen act of aggression, the CCG obstructed the AFP's critical humanitarian rotation and resupply operations at BRP Sierra Madre (LS57) in Ayungin Shoal on June 17, employing physical attacks, bladed weapons, blaring sirens, and blinding strobe lights.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/EROR1.jpg","image_caption":"The windshield, communications and navigational equipment were intentionally destroyed by the CCG when they forcibly towed and looted the AFP’s 9-meter Rigid Hull Inflatable Boat during a humanitarian rotation and resupply mission at BRP Sierra Madre in Ayungin Shoal on June 17.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-19T11:51:26+08:00","hits":1367},{"id":447,"title":"LOOK | Incident during RoRe mission on June 17","slug":"look-incident-during-rore-mission-on-june-17","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The China Coast Guard's coercive, aggressive, and barbaric actions during the humanitarian rotation and resupply mission at BRP Sierra Madre in Ayungin Shoal on June 17, resulted in severe damage to AFP vessels, including their communication and navigation equipment.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CCG personnel were also caught on camera while brandishing an assortment of bladed and pointed weapons threatening to injure AFP troops.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The core issue remains the illegal presence and activities of China within our jurisdiction. The continued hostile behavior of the CCG is what escalates tensions in the area.</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/EROR6.jpg","image_caption":"A CCG personnel was caught on camera while threatening to injure an AFP soldier with a pickaxe during the humanitarian rotation and resupply mission at BRP Sierra Madre in Ayungin Shoal on June 17.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-19T11:39:00+08:00","hits":1477},{"id":448,"title":"VCSAFP welcomes U.S. 7th Fleet Commander","slug":"vcsafp-welcomes-u-s-7th-fleet-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – LtGen Arthur Cordura, Vice Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, welcomed Vice Admiral Frederick William Kacher, Commander, U.S. 7th Fleet, during his courtesy visit on June 19, 2024, here.<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">During the meeting, LtGen Cordura and Vice Admiral Kacher discussed the current security environment and reaffirmed their commitment to upholding rules-based international law to promote a free and prosperous Indo-Pacific region. They also discussed their progressive engagements in multilateral partnerships that aim to advance collective maritime domain security.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/WEL4.jpg","image_caption":"AFP's Vice Chief of Staff LtGen Arthur Cordura, Vice Admiral Frederick William Kacher, Commander, U.S. 7th Fleet, along with key officials pose for a photo during the latter's courtesy visit on June 19, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-19T11:36:01+08:00","hits":1149},{"id":449,"title":"On the Humanitarian Rotation and Resupply Mission at BRP Sierra Madre on June 17.","slug":"on-the-humanitarian-rotation-and-resupply-mission-at-brp-sierra-madre-on-june-17","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <p>Statement of the Armed Forces of the Philippines on the Humanitarian Rotation and Resupply Mission at BRP Sierra Madre on June 17.</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/rore.jpg","image_caption":"Statement of the Armed Forces of the Philippines on the Humanitarian Rotation and Resupply Mission at BRP Sierra Madre on June 17.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-18T09:04:45+08:00","hits":1083},{"id":450,"title":"AFP welcomes new Army officers","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-army-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines welcomed new officers with the graduation of Officer Candidate Course (OCC) Class 60-2024 on June 15, 2024, at Camp O'Donnell, Tarlac City.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/PAOF.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr bestows the Chief of Staff Saber to 2Lt Ariela Garras during the graduation ceremony of the Officer Candidate Course Class 60-2024 on June 15 in Camp O'Donnell, Tarlac City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-15T09:33:13+08:00","hits":1144},{"id":451,"title":"PAF holds 2024 Symposium and Expo, pursues adaptive resilience","slug":"paf-holds-2024-symposium-and-expo-pursues-adaptive-resilience","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City –The Philippine Air Force (PAF) held a successful culmination of the Symposium and Expo 2024, highlighting the pursuit of adaptive resilience. General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, graced the event as the Guest of Honor and Speaker on June 14, 2024, at Manila Marriot Hotel, Pasay City.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/SYM1.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, assisted by LtGen Stephen Parreño, Commander General, PAF, during the Air Force Symposium and Expo 2024 on June 14, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-14T09:30:20+08:00","hits":942},{"id":452,"title":"Military discipline, competence shine in Independence Day parade","slug":"military-discipline-competence-shine-in-independence-day-parade","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The 126th anniversary of Philippine Independence was marked with a parade featuring various military units and personnel from other uniformed services at the Quirino Grandstand in Manila on June 12.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/PRADE.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand Marcos Jr and the first family, along with other dignitaries, witness the parade in commemoration of the 126th anniversary of the Philippine Independence on June 12 at the Quirino Grandstand in Manila City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-12T09:39:39+08:00","hits":1346},{"id":453,"title":"AFP joins 126th Philippine Independence Day rites","slug":"afp-joins-126th-philippine-independence-day-rites","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines participated in the 126th anniversary of Philippine Independence, culminating in the Simultaneous Flag Raising &amp; Wreath Laying ceremony led by President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. at the Rizal National Monument in Manila City.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/IDAY.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand Marcos Jr marches with AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr during the Simultaneous Flag-raising and Wreath-laying Ceremony at the Rizal National Monument in commemoration of the 126th anniversary of the Philippine Independence on June 12.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-12T09:37:13+08:00","hits":1033},{"id":454,"title":"President Marcos Jr visits troops in North Luzon, orders preparation","slug":"president-marcos-jr-visits-troops-in-north-luzon-orders-preparation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—President Ferdinand Marcos Jr visited the troops of the 5th Infantry Division and Joint Task Force Tala in their headquarters in Gamu, Isabela on June 10 where he ordered military units to prepare for external threats.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/5ID.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand Marcos Jr poses for a photo during his visit to the 5th Infantry Division in Gamu, Isabela on June 10.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-11T09:33:58+08:00","hits":857},{"id":455,"title":"On the 126th Anniversary of the Philippine Independence","slug":"on-the-126th-anniversary-of-the-philippine-independence","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/viber_image_2024-06-11_08-11-20-097.jpg","image_caption":"Message of General Romeo S Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, on the 126th Anniversary of the Philippine Independence.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-11T09:26:28+08:00","hits":184},{"id":456,"title":"PH-US-AUS-JP top military officials meet in Singapore","slug":"ph-us-aus-jp-top-military-officials-meet-in-singapore","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), met with his counterparts from the United States, Japan, and Australia at the sidelines of the Shangri-La Dialogue in Singapore on May 31.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/sing.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), met with his counterparts from the United States, Japan, and Australia at the sidelines of the Shangri-La Dialogue in Singapore on May 31.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-07T09:50:59+08:00","hits":467},{"id":457,"title":"AFP installs new EASTMINCOM commander","slug":"afp-installs-new-eastmincom-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines installed MGen Luis Rex Bergante as the new commander of Eastern Mindanao Command (EASTMINCOM) in a Change of Command ceremony on June 7 in Davao City.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/EMC2.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, hands over the command flag to MGen Luis Rex Bergante during the Eastern Mindanao Command Change of Command ceremony on June 7 in Davao City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-07T09:47:32+08:00","hits":1225},{"id":458,"title":"AFP, RTU signs MOU, strengthen research and development","slug":"afp-rtu-signs-mou-strengthen-research-and-development","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines and Rizal Technological University (RTU) held a Ceremonial Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) for strengthening research and development on June 6, 2024, at Boni Avenue, Mandaluyong City.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/RTU2.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Arvin Lagamon, Deputy Chief of Staff for Civil-Military Operations, J7, and Dr. Ma. Eugenia Yangco, RTU President, during the signing ceremony on June 6, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-06T09:42:27+08:00","hits":462},{"id":459,"title":"AFP Launches Regular Zumba Activity for Civilian Human Resources","slug":"afp-launches-regular-zumba-activity-for-civilian-human-resources","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) launched its regular Zumba activity for its civilian human resources (Civ HRs) on June 4 with the Chief of Staff AFP General Romeo Brawner Jr serving as the guest of honor and speaker.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/ZUM.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, performs with the participants of the launching of the Zumba activity for civilian human resources on June 4 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-04T14:45:33+08:00","hits":361},{"id":460,"title":"Statement of the Armed Forces of the Philippines on the Alleged Gun-pointing Incident at BRP Sierra Madre.","slug":"statement-of-the-armed-forces-of-the-philippines-on-the-alleged-gun-pointing-incident-at-brp-sierra-madre","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    ","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/GP.jpg","image_caption":"Statement of the Armed Forces of the Philippines on the Alleged Gun-pointing Incident at BRP Sierra Madre.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-04T14:42:15+08:00","hits":236},{"id":461,"title":"AFP ramps up security measures","slug":"afp-ramps-up-security-measures","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) has announced the implementation of heightened security measures across its military camps as a testament to the AFP's commitment to the PH-US General Security of Military Information Agreement (GSOMIA) aimed at fortifying bilateral relations and enhancing overall security capabilities.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/GSOM.jpg","image_caption":"K9 and Explosive Ordnance Disposal teams complement ingress and egress security measures at all camp gates of Camp General Emilio Aguinaldo, Quezon City. Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-03T14:39:33+08:00","hits":628},{"id":462,"title":"AFP props troops’ role in regional peace, stability","slug":"afp-props-troops-role-in-regional-peace-stability","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br /><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—Following President Ferdinand Marcos Jr’s historic speech at the Shangri-La Dialogue, the Armed Forces of the Philippines echoed the importance of the open, inclusive, and rules-based international order and the role of military and civilian personnel of the AFP in its success.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/FR3.jpg","image_caption":"Senior military officers and enlisted leaders of the General Headquarters render their salute during Monday's flag-raising ceremony on June 3 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-03T14:37:08+08:00","hits":207},{"id":463,"title":"AFP appoints Acting EASTMINCOM Commander","slug":"afp-appoints-acting-eastmincom-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -- The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Eastern Mindanao Command (EASTMINCOM) held a Retirement and Change of Command Ceremony to appoint Major General Jose Maria Cuerpo II as its acting Commander, replacing Lieutenant General Greg Almerol who relinquished his post after reaching mandatory retirement age.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The ceremony was presided over by Lieutenant General Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, representing the AFP Chief of Staff on May 31, 2024 at the Naval Station Felix Apolinario in Camp Panacan, Davao City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/EMC.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Greg Almerol relinquishes his post to MGen Jose Maria Cuerpo II who will take over in an acting capacity through a Change of Command Ceremony for EASTMINCOM as presided over by The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-06-01T10:30:45+08:00","hits":2572},{"id":464,"title":"AFP welcomes new Provost Marshal General","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-provost-marshal-general","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) installed Marine Colonel Ferdinand Marcelino as the new The Provost Marshal General (TPMG) AFP in a Change of Chief of Office and Retirement Ceremony on May 31 in Tejeros Hall here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/June%202024/prov1.jpg","image_caption":"Col Ferdinand Marcelino, the new The Provost Marshal General (TPMG) AFP, receives the office symbol of TPMG during the Change of Chief of Office on May 31 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-31T10:28:23+08:00","hits":3248},{"id":465,"title":"AFP Chief welcomes US Army Pacific Commanding General, strengthens bilateral relations","slug":"afp-chief-welcomes-us-army-pacific-commanding-general-strengthens-bilateral-relations","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br /><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – General Romeo Brawner Jr., Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), welcomed General Charles Flynn, Commanding General, US Army Pacific, on an office call fostering stronger ties, here on April 30, 2024.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The meeting highlighted AFP's optimism in the longstanding PH-US alliance. It reaffirmed the commitment to strengthen defense cooperation and stressed the shared dedication to promoting peace, stability, and prosperity.<br />","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/CALL.jpg","image_caption":"General Brawner Jr., CSAFP, welcomes General Flynn, Commanding General of the US Army Pacific, during the latter’s office call on April 30, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-30T10:42:02+08:00","hits":3919},{"id":466,"title":"AFP signs DOC, empowering local communities","slug":"afp-signs-doc-empowering-local-communities","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines signed a Declaration of Cooperation (DOC) of a joint forum/workshop empowering local communities through a Multi-Sector Governance Council Meeting (MSGC), on May 28, 2024 in Headquarters 2nd Marine Brigade, Bongao, Tawi-Tawi.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/DOC1.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff of the AFP, is accorded with arrival honors during the Signing of the Declaration of Cooperation for Joint Forum/Workshop on May 28, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-29T07:18:53+08:00","hits":400},{"id":467,"title":"AFP joins CGEASH 29th Founding Anniversary","slug":"afp-joins-cgeash-29th-founding-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines joined the Camp General Emilio Aguinaldo Station Hospital (CGEASH) on its 29th Founding Anniversary celebration with BGen Fatima Claire Navarro MC, The Surgeon General, AFP, as Guest of Honor on May 29, 2024, here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/CGEA4.jpg","image_caption":"BGen Fatima Claire Navarro MC, The Surgeon General, AFP, along with CGEASH personnel gather for a photo opportunity during its 29th Founding Anniversary on May 29, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-29T07:16:33+08:00","hits":650},{"id":468,"title":"PBBM SENDOFF TO BRUNEI AND SINGAPORE","slug":"pbbm-sendoff-to-brunei-and-singapore","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">LOOK | General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, along with top military and government officials, join the sendoff for President Ferdinand Marcos Jr and First Lady Liza Araneta Marcos in their state visit to Brunei and working visit to Singapore on May 28 to 31, 2024. Among his agenda is the Shangri-La Dialogue where he will deliver the keynote address.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">“I think it is extremely timely that I attend and put forward and articulate the Philippines’ perspectives and outlook on defense and diplomacy while we continue to highlight the Philippines’ commitment to a rules-based international order and constructive multilateralism amidst the current geopolitical challenges that we face in our region,” President Marcos said.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Photo by SSg Ambay/PAOAFP</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/SEO.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, along with top military and government officials, join the sendoff for President Ferdinand Marcos Jr and First Lady Liza Araneta Marcos in their state visit to Brunei and working visit to Singapore on May 28 to 31, 2024. Among his agenda is the Shangri-La Dialogue where he will deliver the keynote address. ","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-28T15:17:05+08:00","hits":312},{"id":469,"title":"AFP joins US Memorial Day rites","slug":"afp-joins-us-memorial-day-rites","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined the United States Embassy and other dignitaries in a solemn ceremony to commemorate Memorial Day at the Manila American Cemetery and Memorial on May 26. The event honored the valor and sacrifice of the American and Filipino soldiers who fought together during World War II.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/MEM5.jpg","image_caption":"Undersecretary of National Defense Irineo Espino joins US officials in the wreath-laying ceremony during the US Memorial Day rites at the Manila American Cemetery and Memorial on May 26.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-27T02:17:26+08:00","hits":284},{"id":470,"title":"CSAFP leads awarding ceremony for outgoing UP ROTC cadet officers","slug":"csafp-leads-awarding-ceremony-for-outgoing-up-rotc-cadet-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, led on May 25 the awarding ceremony for the outgoing cadet officers of University of the Philippines Reserve Officers Training Corps.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/rotcup%201.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, confers the Military Merit Medal to Cadet Major Stephanie Ann Gutierrez 1CL during the 102nd Homecoming of the UP Vanguard on May 25 at the University of the Philippines Diliman campus.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-26T10:18:02+08:00","hits":290},{"id":471,"title":"AFP Reservist Run Marks AFPRESCOM's 31st Anniversary","slug":"afp-reservist-run-marks-afprescoms-31st-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—Runners of all ages and abilities gathered in the Armed Forces of the Philippines Reservist Run held May 25 here that marked the 31st founding anniversary of the AFP Reserve Command (AFPRESCOM).<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Themed \"AFPRESCOM @31: Overcoming challenges, building resilience, and sustaining excellence,\" the event featured three race categories—10 km, 5 km, and 3 km.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">AFPRESCOM is dedicated to developing and maintaining a capable and responsive reserve force, committed to supporting the regular armed forces in times of need and engaging in various community service initiatives.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Founded 31 years ago, AFPRESCOM continues to play a crucial role in national defense and community development through its robust training programs and outreach efforts.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">As the organization looks forward to another year of service, the funds raised will be instrumental in enhancing the capabilities of reservists and expanding outreach programs, further solidifying the link between the armed forces and the communities they protect.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photo by SSg Amagan/PAOAFP)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/frun%201.jpg","image_caption":"Runners in the 10km category head out from the start line of the AFP Reservist Run held in celebration of the 31st Anniversary of the AFP Reserve Command on May 25 at Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-25T10:15:26+08:00","hits":273},{"id":472,"title":"AFP reps join Public Affairs Course at US’ Defense Information School","slug":"afp-reps-join-public-affairs-course-at-us-defense-information-school","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City – Representatives from the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) completed the five-week Public Affairs Course for International Students (PACIS) last May 17 at Fort Meade, Maryland, USA.<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Major Gil Gamay of the Philippine Army and Mr. Redentor Reyes of the Public Affairs Office AFP, who was recognized as a Distinguished Honor Graduate, joined seven other students from South Korea, Zambia, Slovenia, Italy, Jordan, and Brazil in the program.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/RR%201.jpg","image_caption":"Students of the Public Affairs Course for International Students 2024 presents a memento to Mr Rivers Johnson, International Military Students Officer of the Defense Information School, on May 17 at Fort Meade, Maryland, USA.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-24T10:13:17+08:00","hits":283},{"id":473,"title":"AFP joins Philippine Navy 126th Anniversary","slug":"afp-joins-philippine-navy-126th-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines joined in the celebration of the 126th Anniversary of the Philippine Navy on May 24, 2024, at its Headquarters in Roxas Blvd, Manila.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/SN3.jpg","image_caption":"Secretary of National Defense Gilberto Teodoro Jr. and General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, along with Philippine Navy personnel gather for a photo opportunity during the 126th Anniversary celebration of the Philippine Navy on May 24, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-24T10:11:28+08:00","hits":284},{"id":474,"title":"AFP Chief joins PBBM on beneficial visit to Tawi-Tawi","slug":"afp-chief-joins-pbbm-on-beneficial-visit-to-tawi-tawi","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, joined President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. on a beneficial visit to Tawi-Tawi on May 23, 2024.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/TAW3.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, receives President Ferdinand Marcos Jr., during the arrival honors for his visit to Tawi-Tawi on May 23, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-23T10:08:35+08:00","hits":180},{"id":475,"title":"AFP conducts groundbreaking ceremony for new OLA building","slug":"afp-conducts-groundbreaking-ceremony-for-new-ola-building","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines conducted the groundbreaking ceremony of the new building of the Office for Legislative Affairs (OLA) on May 23, 2024, here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/GR4.jpg","image_caption":"BGen Armand Arevalo, Commander, GHQ, and HSC, and Hon. Raul “Boboy” Tupas, 5th District Representative, Iloilo, along with AFP personnel, lead the groundbreaking ceremony of the new OLA building, on May 23, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-23T10:05:02+08:00","hits":485},{"id":476,"title":"AFP welcomes new Deputy Chief of Staff for Operations","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-deputy-chief-of-staff-for-operations","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines formally welcomed BGen Jimmy Larida PN(M) as the new Deputy Chief of Staff for Operations, J3, in a Change of Chief of Office Ceremony, presided over by LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan PN(M), The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, on May 21, 2024, here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/CHAN%201.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, and incoming DCS for Operations, J3, BGen Jimmy Larida, along with AFP key officers, pose for a photo during the Change of Chief of Office Ceremony on May 21, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-21T09:52:56+08:00","hits":2702},{"id":477,"title":"33 AFP senior officers get CA approval","slug":"33-afp-senior-officers-get-ca-approval","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Commission on Appointments approved the ad interim promotion of 33 military officers during the plenary session and deliberation in Pasay City on May 21.<br /></span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/SEN4.jpg","image_caption":"AFP senior officers pose for a photo with Commission on Appointments headed by Senate President Francis Escudero on May 21.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-21T09:49:40+08:00","hits":563},{"id":478,"title":"CSAFP leads handover and blessing ceremony for TIKAS projects","slug":"csafp-leads-handover-and-blessing-ceremony-for-tikas-projects","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – General Romeo Brawner Jr., Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff, led the handover and blessing ceremony of the newly established HMPG Multi-Purpose Barracks, GHQ Function Hall, CGEA Firing Range Function Hall, and J. Fernando Road under the Tatag ng Imprastraktura para sa Kapayapaan at Seguridad (TIKAS) Convergence Program on May 21, 2024, here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/TIK3.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, and Senator Mark Villar during the ribbon-cutting ceremony of the newly asphalted J. Fernando Road on May 21, 2024 at Camp Aguinaldo.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-21T09:46:47+08:00","hits":411},{"id":479,"title":"Army Reserve Command inaugurates new battalion headquarters","slug":"army-reserve-command-inaugurates-new-battalion-headquarters","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Army Reserve Command (ARESCOM) celebrated the blessing and inauguration of the new headquarters of the 1304th Ready Reserve Infantry (The Fort) Battalion (RRIBn) located at Cuartel de Sta. Lucia, Intramuros, Manila last May 20, 2024.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/ARES4.jpg","image_caption":"AFP officers and DOT Secretary Christina Garcia-Frasco presented with new materials and supplies for the new headquarters of the 1304th Ready Reserve Infantry (The Fort) Battalion on May 20, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-21T09:44:59+08:00","hits":889},{"id":480,"title":"CSAFP welcomes U.S. Pacific Fleet Commander","slug":"csafp-welcomes-u-s-pacific-fleet-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – General Romeo Brawner Jr., Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), welcomed Admiral Stephen Koehler, Commander, United States Pacific Fleet, during a courtesy visit on May 20, 2024, here.<br /></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/CCAL1.jpg","image_caption":"Admiral Stephen Koehler, Commander, United States Pacific Fleet, is accorded with arrival honors led by General Romeo Brawner Jr., Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), during the former’s courtesy visit on May 20, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-21T09:41:14+08:00","hits":295},{"id":481,"title":"AFP commends Affiliated Reserve Unit Commanders in leadership convention","slug":"afp-commends-affiliated-reserve-unit-commanders-in-leadership-convention","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) awarded deserving Commanders of AFP Affiliated Reserve Units (AFPARU) during a convention held here on May 17, 2024.<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Lieutenant General Arthur M Cordura, the AFP Vice Chief of Staff, graced the event as the Guest of Honor and Speaker. In his keynote address, LtGen Cordura recognized the exemplary contributions of the AFPARU in supporting the AFP's mission and enhancing the country's overall security framework.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/res.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Joel Alejandro S Nacnac, Deputy Chief of Staff for Reservist and Retiree Affairs, J9 and LtGen Arthur M Cordura, Vice Chief of Staff, AFP, together with the participants of the AFPARU Commanders Convention in Camp Aguinaldo on May 17, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-17T09:39:04+08:00","hits":254},{"id":482,"title":"AFP Chief joins awarding ceremony of PMA Class of 2024","slug":"afp-chief-joins-awarding-ceremony-of-pma-class-of-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The AFP Chief of Staff, General Romeo Brawner Jr., graced the awarding ceremony for outstanding cadets and units of the Cadet Corps, AFP (CCAFP) on May 17, 2024, at Philippine Military Academy, Fort Gregorio H Del Pilar, Baguio City.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/pma.jpg","image_caption":"Secretary Teodoro Jr. of the Department of National Defense; AFP Chief of Staff, General Brawner Jr; and PMA Superintendent LtGen Tolentino, along with the PMA \"Bagong Sinag\"  Class of 2024 awardees gather for a photo opportunity on May 17, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-17T09:36:39+08:00","hits":548},{"id":483,"title":"AFP's GHQ & HSC celebrates 37th Founding Anniversary","slug":"afps-ghq-hsc-celebrates-37th-founding-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The General Headquarters and Headquarters Service Command (GHQ &amp; HSC), AFP celebrated its 37th founding anniversary with a theme, \"Bagong Camp Aguinaldo, Bagong Pilipinas\" on May 15, 2024, here.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/SD.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Arthur Cordura, AFP Vice Chief of Staff, and the GHQ & HSC member awardees gather for a photo opportunity on May 15, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-17T09:33:02+08:00","hits":292},{"id":484,"title":"AFP welcomes the Swedish delegates","slug":"afp-welcomes-the-swedish-delegates","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines welcomed Brigadier General Olle Hultgren, Swedish Military Adviser of the Department for Armament and Industry Ministry of Defense, during a courtesy visit. He was met by LtGen Steve Crespillo, The Inspector General, AFP, on May 15, 2024, here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">LtGen Crespillo expressed optimism with BGen Hultgren about the prospects for further collaboration and looked forward to advancing shared pursuit in defense and security. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/d.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Steve Crespillo, The Inspector General, AFP, Brigadier General Olle Hultgren, along with AFP key officers and Swedish delegates, pose for a photo opportunity on May 15, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-15T09:58:12+08:00","hits":2050},{"id":485,"title":"CSAFP dons new rank to newly promoted general","slug":"csafp-dons-new-rank-to-newly-promoted-general","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – General Romeo Brawner Jr., the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, donned new rank to LtGen Facundo Palafox IV, Commander, Southern Luzon Command (SOLCOM), in a ceremony on May 15, 2024, here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">LtGen Palafox is a proud member of PMA Bigkis-Lahi Class of 1990 and has been assigned to various key units of the Philippine Army and the AFP. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/PAL2.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Facundo Palafox IV being donned new ranks by General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, and Ms Anna Lissa A Palafox on May 15, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-15T09:55:49+08:00","hits":4568},{"id":486,"title":"CSAFP welcomes newly promoted officers ","slug":"csafp-welcomes-newly-promoted-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — General Romeo Brawner Jr., the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), received the 39-newly promoted officers for a courtesy visit after taking oath before the President here on May 13, 2024.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">During the courtesy call, General Brawner Jr. welcomed the newly promoted officers, congratulating them on their well-deserved achievements and reaffirming the AFP's commitment to upholding peace, security, and stability.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/PRO1.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief of Staff, along with 39 newly promoted generals and flag officers, pose for a photo on May 13, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-14T09:51:50+08:00","hits":5904},{"id":487,"title":"PH-US cap Balikatan 2024, mark milestone in defense cooperation","slug":"ph-us-cap-balikatan-2024-mark-milestone-in-defense-cooperation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the United States Armed Forces successfully concluded Balikatan 2024 with a closing ceremony held here on Friday, May 10, 2024, marking the culmination of the most comprehensive iteration of the annual defense exercise yet.<br /><br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The closing ceremony was attended by distinguished guests, with the Secretary of National Defense, Gilberto Teodoro Jr., as Guest of Honor and Speaker, along with the US Ambassador to the Philippines, Her Excellency Marykay Loss Carlson, and AFP Chief of Staff, General Romeo Brawner Jr.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/BKCLOS.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Marvin Licudine, Her Excellency Marykay Loss Carlson, Secretary Gilberto Teodoro Jr., General Romero Brawner Jr., and LtGen Michael Cederholm, gather for a photo opportunity during the Exercise Balikatan 39-2024 closing ceremony on May 10, 2024, at AFPCOC, Camp Aguinaldo.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-10T13:48:17+08:00","hits":3674},{"id":488,"title":"Exercise Balikatan 39-24 showcases joint firepower","slug":"exercise-balikatan-39-24-showcases-joint-firepower","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – In a display of unparalleled interoperability and combined might, Philippine and US forces successfully conducted a maritime strike exercise as part of Balikatan 2024.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/MS1.jpg","image_caption":"AW-109 showcasing its aerial prowess to ensure a safe and secure maritime domain during #Balikatan2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-09T13:46:23+08:00","hits":3291},{"id":489,"title":"PH-US Armed Forces strike mock target, exhibit deterrence capability","slug":"ph-us-armed-forces-strike-mock-target-exhibit-deterrence-capability","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines and the United States Armed Forces successfully executed maritime strike exercises at La Paz Sand Dunes in Laoag on May 8, 2024, as part of the </span><span class=\"html-span xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><a class=\"x1i10hfl xjbqb8w x1ejq31n xd10rxx x1sy0etr x17r0tee x972fbf xcfux6l x1qhh985 xm0m39n x9f619 x1ypdohk xt0psk2 xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x16tdsg8 xggy1nq x1a2a7pz xt0b8zv x1hl2dhg x1fey0fg xo1l8bm\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"link\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/exercisebalikatan?__cft__[0]=AZUmDlltq3rb1Gubji26ADclKc13UBEoblEvMmHkvor4VI3bG8i1CQQ7MGs8kg7ed72hU1CC200OOpNCF_qe3hCqYT1hySt7qGbdH_7bEbd3gJOHtOHd0ebTL2ORcrstv9LYB3pGW4J_jTkDllS2hED9xsoKDCI5Ul2GVeZ1Tt0OM9DeUJeh9PslKWnFZZowapnThmcY0DOqlK_xxOf-jwzV3COQnz88s3k3OROd8xgm1g&amp;__tn__=-]K-R\"><span class=\"xt0psk2\">Exercise Balikatan</span></a></span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"> 39-2024.<br /><br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">A maritime strike exercise is a strategic military operation conducting integrated land, sea, and air platforms to simultaneously sense, target, and strike against simulated targets at sea. This aims to strengthen maritime security capabilities and proficiency in naval interdiction and deterrence operations.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/MARST.jpg","image_caption":"BRP Jose Rizal (FF-150) during the Maritime Strike Exercise of the #Balikatan2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-08T16:43:12+08:00","hits":3219},{"id":490,"title":"AFP Statement on Chinese Embassy in Manila’s claim of a “new model” of conduct in the West Philippines Sea.","slug":"afp-statement-on-chinese-embassy-in-manila-s-claim-of-a-new-model-of-conduct-in-the-west-philippines-sea","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"        <p>AFP Statement on Chinese Embassy in Manila’s claim of a “new model” of conduct in the West Philippines Sea.</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/NM.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Statement on Chinese Embassy in Manila’s claim of a “new model” of conduct in the West Philippines Sea.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-08T13:44:33+08:00","hits":3185},{"id":491,"title":"Joint PH-US Military Drill Simulates Repelling Beach Landing","slug":"joint-ph-us-military-drill-simulates-repelling-beach-landing","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"html-div xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd\">\r\n<div class=\"html-div xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm x1mh8g0r x18d9i69 x1cy8zhl x78zum5 x1q0g3np xod5an3 x1pi30zi x1swvt13 xz9dl7a\">\r\n<div class=\"html-div xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1iyjqo2\">\r\n<div class=\"x78zum5 xdt5ytf xz62fqu x16ldp7u\">\r\n<div class=\"xu06os2 x1ok221b\"> </div>\r\n<div class=\"xu06os2 x1ok221b\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines and the United States Armed Forces successfully conducted counter-landing exercises at La Paz Sand Dunes in Laoag on May 6, 2024, as part of the </span><span class=\"html-span xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><a class=\"x1i10hfl xjbqb8w x1ejq31n xd10rxx x1sy0etr x17r0tee x972fbf xcfux6l x1qhh985 xm0m39n x9f619 x1ypdohk xt0psk2 xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x16tdsg8 xggy1nq x1a2a7pz xt0b8zv x1hl2dhg x1fey0fg xo1l8bm\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"link\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/exercisebalikatan?__cft__[0]=AZWvlgXrq7T0XTfut10oPYJpFEvhwf9LJXIbsPB1ILEi2f6T8L-XenYSnW6Aq-AAtwsZ60Awg990TKkhIfpVf4EbjDzEuSii0rqq8h21c8A1hdRQYJgx_kvW4wMVeKP6TiUW7FzRsUajBFajnSiAtWten_eAPPFG8nsuuFidM2Q99s3ugCvw7Gza29-q1j-4FBLFOoyPUPEFSDpNKOxE1kjO4BaoYeNHiJY4U_4lhXgSMA&amp;__tn__=-]K-R\"><span class=\"xt0psk2\">Exercise Balikatan</span></a></span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"> 39-2024.</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"xu06os2 x1ok221b\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"html-div xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd\">\r\n<div class=\"html-div xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd\" dir=\"auto\">\r\n<div id=\":rts:\" class=\"x1iorvi4 x1pi30zi x1l90r2v x1swvt13\" data-ad-comet-preview=\"message\" data-ad-preview=\"message\">\r\n<div class=\"x78zum5 xdt5ytf xz62fqu x16ldp7u\">\r\n<div class=\"xu06os2 x1ok221b\">\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Counter-landing live-fire operation is a military strategy that involves deploying defensive forces, such as infantry and artillery to deter hostile forces seeking to establish presence within the nation's borders.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/COUNTER%20LANDING.jpg","image_caption":"Filipino troops showcase their capabilities and modern assets during the Counter Landing Live Fire Exercises of Balikatan 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-06T13:41:26+08:00","hits":3307},{"id":492,"title":"U.S. Marines, Philippine Air Force conduct HADR training in Palawan","slug":"u-s-marines-philippine-air-force-conduct-hadr-training-in-palawan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The U.S. Marines and the Philippine Air Force's Tactical Operations Wing West (TOW-WEST) joined forces for a Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Response (HADR) Subject Matter Expert Exchange (SMEE) in Antonio Bautista Air Base, Puerto Princesa City on May 3, 2024.<br /></span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/hadrpal.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-04T13:39:31+08:00","hits":3325},{"id":493,"title":"Live Fire Exercises showcase HIMARS, coastal defense abilities","slug":"live-fire-exercises-showcase-himars-coastal-defense-abilities","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -- On May 2nd, the combined forces of the Philippine Marine Corps (PMC) and the United States Marine Corps (USMC) conducted a successful live-fire exercise as part of </span><span class=\"html-span xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><a class=\"x1i10hfl xjbqb8w x1ejq31n xd10rxx x1sy0etr x17r0tee x972fbf xcfux6l x1qhh985 xm0m39n x9f619 x1ypdohk xt0psk2 xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x16tdsg8 xggy1nq x1a2a7pz xt0b8zv x1hl2dhg x1fey0fg xo1l8bm\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"link\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/exercisebalikatan?__cft__[0]=AZWGyT2hd0suASb5bl_4GOgMxqWaduv5lWQkF3QMVB7JzhfZs4Xw9gYc7UAItaYbEz9OPoOzmjSW51EFS_JQAU6LWrbYQrhruG2MNjHwab5yPa0eNTNpNUgfSjeQJVpORxAWpSfZU4B_yhhPXdkNTb_JVMumTbdqqTjMUD0aAME-HVfD2c0mnG4SK2U3yvbebXLhU8wS991OyCFlYHhDwAGvUTGHQH9ZBaD6bWUEKzK18w&amp;__tn__=-]K-R\"><span class=\"xt0psk2\">Exercise Balikatan</span></a></span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">. The exercise, held at Campong Ulay in the coastal town of Rizal, Palawan, showcased the capabilities of the High Mobility Artillery Rocket System (HIMARS) and other key assets in a simulated coastal defense scenario.<br /><br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The day began with a booming display of HIMARS firing several rockets at mock targets in the West Philippine Sea (WPS). The precision and long-range hitting capabilities of this state-of-the-art artillery system demonstrated its importance in contemporary conflict scenarios.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/CD.jpg","image_caption":"A rocket fired towards designated targets within the West Philippine Sea (WPS) from HIMARS launchers during the Live Fire Exercises of #Balikatan2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-03T13:38:06+08:00","hits":3071},{"id":494,"title":"TDCSAFP welcomes new Deputy Chief of Staff for Operations","slug":"tdcsafp-welcomes-new-deputy-chief-of-staff-for-operations","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City- LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP), on behalf of AFP Chief General Romeo Brawner Jr., welcomed Acting Deputy Chief of Staff for Operations Commodore Peter Jempsun De Guzman, as he assumed office succeeding LtGen Fernando Reyeg, here on May 03, 2024.<br /><br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">During the ceremony, LtGen Gaerlan honored LtGen Reyeg for his expertise and exemplary service, which has been significant in OJ3’s successful operations over the years. He also commended LtGen Reyeg for his leadership in crafting and executing various programs and organization developments, such as the publication of the AFP Territorial Defense Plan “Bantay Kalayaan,” which served as a strategic guidance for the AFP in securing the nation’s territorial integrity and maritime sovereignty.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/OJ3.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Gaerlan, AFP Deputy Chief of Staff, Acting Deputy Chief of Staff for Operations Commodore De Guzman, LtGen Fernando Reyeg, pose for a photo opportunity during the OJ3 Change of Chief of Office Ceremony on May 03, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-03T13:35:27+08:00","hits":4363},{"id":495,"title":"AFP conducts Aerial Resupply exercise at Patag Island in West Philippine Sea","slug":"afp-conducts-aerial-resupply-exercise-at-patag-island-in-west-philippine-sea","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) successfully conducted an aerial resupply operation at Patag Island on April 27, 2024. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Philippine Air Force NC212i aircraft was used to deliver essential goods to include food and medicine to government troops deployed on the remote island. The exercise aimed to conduct aerial resupply operation in two separate cargo drop scenarios; utilizing a parachute directly onto the island and cargo drop into the sea for retrieval by the stationed personnel.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/ARESU.jpg","image_caption":"A Philippine Marine aboard the Philippine Air Force NC212i aircraft drops the second cargo onto the sea for the retrieval of personnel stationed at Patag Island on April 27, 2024. (Photo by AFP Western Command)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-01T10:54:23+08:00","hits":3890},{"id":496,"title":"Filipino troops observe U.S. Army's Medical Capabilities in Cagayan","slug":"filipino-troops-observe-u-s-armys-medical-capabilities-in-cagayan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Members of the Forward Service Medical Company (FSMC) under the 5th Infantry Division, Philippine Army, actively participated in a capability demonstration organized by the 10th Field Hospital of the United States Army at the Cagayan North International Airport in Lal-lo, Cagayan on Monday, April 29.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The demonstration sought to foster knowledge exchange and enhance interoperability between the AFP and the U.S. Army. FSMC personnel were able to observe and engage with their U.S. Army counterparts, gaining valuable insights into the latest medical practices and techniques used in military operations.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/MCC.jpg","image_caption":"FSMC personnel interact with their U.S. Army counterparts during the medical capability demonstration at the Cagayan North International Airport in Lal-lo, Cagayan on April 29, 2024. (Photo by AFP Northern Luzon Command)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-01T10:52:39+08:00","hits":4386},{"id":497,"title":"Filipino, American para-jumpers hold successful Military Free Fall exercise in Palawan","slug":"filipino-american-para-jumpers-hold-successful-military-free-fall-exercise-in-palawan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – A successful Military Free Fall (MFF) Jump Exercise was conducted in Long Beach, San Vicente, Palawan on April 30, 2024, as part of the 39th annual Balikatan Exercise between the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the United States Indo-Pacific Command (US-INDOPACOM).<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Para-jumpers from the Philippine Marine Corps Reconnaissance, Special Operations Wing of the Philippine Air Force, Special Forces Regiment Airborne, and their U.S. counterparts took part in the exercise. Members from the Australian Defence Force also joined as observers. The MFF Jump was a key component of the Balikatan Exercise, emphasizing the importance of interoperability and joint training.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/May%202024/MFF.jpg","image_caption":"A Filipino military para-jumper carries the Philippine Flag as he descends from a U.S. Air Force Special Operations Command MC-130J at Long Beach, San Vicente, Palawan during the military free fall jump exercise on Tuesday, April 30. (Photo by WESCOM, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-05-01T10:51:00+08:00","hits":3972},{"id":498,"title":"TDCSAFP honors AFPRESCOM for three decades of dedicated service","slug":"tdcsafp-honors-afprescom-for-three-decades-of-dedicated-service","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City –LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP), honored the AFP Reserve Command (AFPRESCOM) for its 31st founding anniversary marking three decades of dedicated service here on April 30, 2024.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">AFPRESCOM plays a pivotal role in supporting the AFP's mission to protect the Filipino people and in upholding the nation’s integrity. Over the past 31 years, AFPRESCOM has continuously evolved, adapted to emerging security challenges, and enhanced its readiness to respond to various contingencies.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/AFPRES%201.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Gaerlan, TDCSAFP, BGen Vicente Ronatay, Commander AFPRESCOM, and its personnel pose for a photo opportunity on April 30, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-30T10:48:13+08:00","hits":3744},{"id":499,"title":"AFP Inspector General welcomes UNCMAC Senior Member","slug":"afp-inspector-general-welcomes-uncmac-senior-member","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – LtGen Steve Crespillo, Inspector General of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, welcomed MGen Kang In Kyu, Senior Member of the United Nations Command Military Armistice Commission (UNCMAC), on a courtesy visit marking a significant moment of diplomatic engagement and cooperation on April 30, 2024, here.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The courtesy visit provided an exchange of views on a range of topics, including regional security challenges, humanitarian assistance, disaster relief operations, and potential areas for enhanced cooperation.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/UNCMAC.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Crespillo, Inspector General of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, and MGen Kang, Senior Member of the UNCMAC, pose for a photo opportunity on April 30, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-30T10:44:34+08:00","hits":3808},{"id":500,"title":"Amphibious Landing Exercise","slug":"amphibious-landing-exercise","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">BRP DAVAO DEL SUR (LD602), serving as the Officer Conducting Serial (OCS) and Commander Amphibious Force (CAF), showcased its operational prowess during the ongoing Exercise Balikatan through successful Well Deck Operations and Amphibious Landing Exercises conducted at the vicinity of Campong Ulay Point, Rizal, Palawan.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/AMPH1.jpg","image_caption":"Exercise Balikatan participants making a triumphant landing at the designated Beach Landing Site in Campong Ulay Point, Rizal, Palawan during the Amphibious Exercise.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-30T10:30:31+08:00","hits":3720},{"id":501,"title":"AFP, US Indo-Pacific Command, and French Navy Conclude Historic Multilateral Maritime Exercise","slug":"afp-us-indo-pacific-command-and-french-navy-conclude-historic-multilateral-maritime-exercise","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -- The first iteration of the Multilateral Maritime Exercise (MME) between the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), the United States Indo-Pacific Command (US-INDOPACOM), and the French Navy concluded on April 29, 2024 in Palawan, marking a historic milestone in regional cooperation and security.</span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Held as part of the ongoing <a class=\"x1i10hfl xjbqb8w x1ejq31n xd10rxx x1sy0etr x17r0tee x972fbf xcfux6l x1qhh985 xm0m39n x9f619 x1ypdohk xt0psk2 xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x16tdsg8 x1hl2dhg xggy1nq x1a2a7pz xt0b8zv x1fey0fg xo1l8bm\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"link\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/exercisebalikatan?__cft__[0]=AZX57zgQmhgxN2elyv0vNWViO2vUsDH8RUpiC-EWUA8j6W1n48QBFJndfc5p_-Nt6r8vPM9th_LIN7lb4AGsuVR-C_ox_EBi9G7CwqUynhIXyxBD1Wcjft70QVTfpQ6oLsKS76nI8BPq0UlQlbk4CS7pzGsySpYm4pS_8jDrlo_9fWBpmkitZMhCkfMbipmlPtQ8Q_AN3hSzu6COu3zsYJlVih30dNRNb9A5MTwIewRsjQ&amp;__tn__=-]K-R\"><span class=\"xt0psk2\">Exercise Balikatan</span></a> 39-24, the week-long event from April 25 to 29, 2024, witnessed active participation from Philippine Navy's offshore patrol vessel BRP Ramon Alcaraz (PS-16) and landing dock BRP Davao Del Sur (LD-602), the US Navy's landing ship dock USS Harpers Ferry (LSD-49), and the French Navy's FS Vendemiaire (FFH-734), a Floreal-class frigate.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/CONC1.jpg","image_caption":"Filipino service members conducting Gunnery Exercises on the last day of the historic Multilateral Maritime Exercise between the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), the United States Indo-Pacific Command (US-INDOPACOM), and the French Navy as part of the #Balikatan2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-29T16:24:14+08:00","hits":3813},{"id":502,"title":"AFP welcomes the Commanding General of the US Army Pacific","slug":"afp-welcomes-the-commanding-general-of-the-us-army-pacific","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - LtGen Arthur Cordura, Vice Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (VCSAFP), on behalf of General Romeo Brawner Jr., AFP Chief, welcomed General Charles Flynn, Commanding General, US Army Pacific, on a courtesy visit here on April 29, 2024.</span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The meeting marked a significant milestone in the longstanding alliance between the AFP and the United States Army, underscoring the mutual commitment to enhancing military collaboration. The two parties had constructive discussions on a wide range of strategic issues, including defense cooperation, multidomain awareness, joint training exercises, and shared regional security challenges.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/USAP1.jpg","image_caption":"General Charles Flynn, Commanding General of the US Army Pacific, discusses the importance of joint military exercises during his courtesy visit on April 29, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-29T10:20:32+08:00","hits":3710},{"id":503,"title":"AFP detects unauthorized presence of China research vessel near Catanduanes","slug":"afp-detects-unauthorized-presence-of-china-research-vessel-near-catanduanes","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -- The Armed Forces of the Philippines  has been monitoring the unauthorized presence of a Chinese-flagged research vessel, \"SHEN KUO,\" in the vicinity northeast of Viga, Catanduanes. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The vessel was first sighted on April 25, 60.9 nautical miles east off Rapu-Rapu Island, Albay. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/CUN.jpg","image_caption":"Chinese-flagged research vessel, \"SHEN KUO,\" loitering in the vicinity northeast of Viga, Catanduanes as spotted by NOMAD N-22 aircraft.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-28T09:44:21+08:00","hits":4909},{"id":504,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff underscores Reserve Force importance in territorial defense at 103rd RRIBn Change of Command Ceremony","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-underscores-reserve-force-importance-in-territorial-defense-at-103rd-rribn-change-of-command-ceremony","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -- In a significant gesture of recognition and support, AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo S Brawner Jr attended the 103rd (La Union) Ready Reserve Infantry Battalion (103rd RRIBn) Change of Command Ceremony on April 27, 2024, at the La Union Convention Center in San Fernando, La Union.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With Major General Romulo A Manuel Jr, PA,  who presided over the ceremony, the event signifies the passing of the baton from outgoing Acting Battalion Commander Colonel Ramon F Laudencia MNSA PA (Res), to the incoming Acting Battalion Commander Lieutenant Colonel Francisco Emmanuel R Ortega III, PA (Res).</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/LU.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo S Brawner Jr onstage with MGen Manuel, Col Laudencia (Res), and LtCol Ortega (Res) during the 103rd (La Union) Ready Reserve Infantry Battalion (103rd RRIbn) Change of Command Ceremony on April 27, 2024, at the La Union Convention Center in San Fernando, La Union.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-28T09:39:15+08:00","hits":4472},{"id":505,"title":"Maritime Search and Rescue Exercise held in West Philippine Sea","slug":"maritime-search-and-rescue-exercise-held-in-west-philippine-sea","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — As part of the Balikatan Exercise 39-2024’s Multilateral Maritime Exercise (MME), the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), the United States Indo-Pacific Command (US-INDOPACOM), and the French Navy conducted a joint Maritime Search and Rescue (MSAR) exercise on April 28 in the West Philippine Sea.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The participating naval ships for the MSAR include the Philippine Navy's offshore patrol vessel BRP Ramon Alcaraz (PS-16) and landing dock BRP Davao Del Sur (LD-602), the US Navy's landing ship dock USS Harpers Ferry (LSD-49), and the French Navy's FS Vendemiaire (FFH-734), a Floreal-class frigate. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/MME3.jpg","image_caption":"Crew member of BRP Davao del Sur utilizing advanced optics during a simulated maritime search and rescue exercise during the 5-day Multilateral Maritime Exercise of the Balikatan 2024. (Photo from LD-602)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-28T01:37:44+08:00","hits":4141}]}